# NuProcKG — public demonstration graph (synthetic)
#
# Built from a synthetic sample and eleven fixed synthetic branch examples. The events, records,
# articles, actors, roles, role claims, occurrence claims, resolution claims and identification
# claims are synthetic, as are the activities that made those claims; the three procurement cases and the descriptions of the project's coding and validation
# activities (models, plans and quality measurements) are real. No real event, article or actor
# is included.
# TBox: NuProc Ontology v0.9.0 (this file does not modify it). Licence: CC BY 4.0.
# The file carries no build time, so building it again gives the same bytes.

@prefix channel: <https://w3id.org/nuproc/channel/> .
@prefix crole: <https://w3id.org/nuproc/counterpartyrole/> .
@prefix dqv: <http://www.w3.org/ns/dqv#> .
@prefix eident: <https://w3id.org/nuproc/engagementidentification/> .
@prefix erole: <https://w3id.org/nuproc/engagementrole/> .
@prefix etype: <https://w3id.org/nuproc/eventtype/> .
@prefix nuproc: <https://w3id.org/nuproc/ns#> .
@prefix obo: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/> .
@prefix otype: <https://w3id.org/nuproc/organizationtype/> .
@prefix prole: <https://w3id.org/nuproc/playerrole/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix rstat: <https://w3id.org/nuproc/resolutionstatus/> .
@prefix srole: <https://w3id.org/nuproc/siderole/> .
@prefix time: <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/actor_registry_resolution> a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "judgement of the actor labels in the actor registry by the author"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The author judged each actor label of the loaded dataset in the actor registry (registry/actor_mentions.csv, registry/actor_registry.csv): its kind and, for an organization, which one; the resolution status follows from them (ADR-0022). Each reference's label-level judgement is a resolution claim generated by this activity, and it is the reference's final claim unless an event-level judgement of a bundled label changed the value (ADR-0043)."@en ;
    prov:qualifiedAssociation <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/actor_registry_resolution/association/rules> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/agent/rule-author> .

<https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/candidate_set_consortium_recheck> a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "re-judgement of the remaining candidate-set events by the author"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The author judged again, blind to the model, the earlier determinations and the event identifiers, the 26 events whose candidate-set label had stayed undetermined, separating 'both acting together as one party' from 'one of the two, not determinable' (CONSORTIUM_RECHECK.md, frozen before judging). 1 event(s) named the candidates acting together; their references resolve to the group organization, and that judgement is their final resolution claim. The others remain candidate-set references. Each re-judgement is a resolution claim generated by this activity (ADR-0043)."@en ;
    prov:qualifiedAssociation <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/candidate_set_consortium_recheck/association/protocol> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/agent/rule-author> ;
    prov:wasInformedBy <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/candidate_set_resolution_validation> .

<https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/candidate_set_resolution_review> a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "review of candidate-set determinations by the author"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Coding protocol v3 leaves to the author the events whose excerpts name an organization outside the candidate set. The author decided them event by event; each decision is a resolution claim generated by this review, and it is the final claim where it changed the model's determination (ADR-0040, ADR-0043)."@en,
        "In this demonstration graph no role claim or reference is linked to this activity: the role values and claims are synthetic and are generated by the synthetic activities."@en ;
    prov:qualifiedAssociation <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/candidate_set_resolution_review/association/protocol> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/agent/rule-author> ;
    prov:wasInformedBy <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/engagement_role_coding_v3> .

<https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/engagement_clustering> a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "Clustering of article-level engagements into engagement-event clusters (source pipeline)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The source pipeline grouped article-level engagements sharing the six-field key of the month-granularity rule into one cluster. Each cluster carries this activity's identification claim (key_based): the cluster stands for one engagement only because its records share the key (ADR-0027, ADR-0044)."@en ;
    prov:qualifiedAssociation <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/engagement_clustering/association/rule> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/agent/source-pipeline-aggregation> .

<https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/engagement_identification_recheck> a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "Re-check of the provisional multi-role engagements by the author"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The author judged, from each cluster's case, channel, event type, counterparty role, actor label and excerpts, without event identifiers, role values or occurrence status, whether each of the 79 clusters that were key-based and reported an engagement in which one organization realized two or more facet roles reports one engagement (verified) or several (merged); where the author could not decide, the clustering claim stays final (ADR-0044; protocol evaluation/coding/v3.0/IDENTIFICATION_RECHECK.md)."@en ;
    prov:qualifiedAssociation <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/engagement_identification_recheck/association/protocol> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/agent/rule-author> .

<https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/engagement_identification_reference> a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "Identification reference from the two coders' answers (validation sample of 150)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Where both coders judged that a sampled cluster's records report one engagement, its identification is verified; where both judged several, merged (VALIDATION_PROTOCOL section 2.5). The reference claim is derived from the two coders' claims and is the final identification claim of the cluster (ADR-0044)."@en ;
    prov:qualifiedAssociation <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/engagement_identification_reference/association/protocol> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/agent/rule-author> .

<https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/engagement_role_validation_reference> a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "adjudicated human reference for the engagement roles of the sampled events"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The reference against which the model coding was scored (VALIDATION_PROTOCOL section 2.4): for each sampled event and role, the value on which the two human coders agreed, or the author's decision from the excerpts where they disagreed (30 cells, decided without the model's per-event values but after the agreement figures had been reported). Its values are the final role values of the 150 sampled events: the author decided this after seeing the validation results, departing from section 2.5 of the protocol, so that the graph carries the checked values; the model's claims remain as claims that were not adopted, and the model is evaluated against its frozen output, not against these final values (ADR-0040)."@en ;
    prov:qualifiedAssociation <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/engagement_role_validation_reference/association/codebook>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/engagement_role_validation_reference/association/protocol> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/agent/rule-author> ;
    prov:wasInformedBy <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/engagement_role_validation_coding_A>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/engagement_role_validation_coding_B> .

<https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/relevance_screening> a nuproc:ScreeningActivity ;
    rdfs:label "relevance screening"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "No coding manual is linked: model_execution_metadata.yaml records a manual input for channel-presence coding and event extraction only."@en,
        "This coding stage does not reproduce: neither seed nor sampling temperature was exposed by the hosted model endpoint, and the harness version was not pinned (ADR-0003)."@en ;
    prov:qualifiedAssociation <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/relevance_screening/association/prompt> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/agent/claude-sonnet-5> ;
    nuproc:usedPromptSpecification <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/prompt/relevance_screening-spec-v1> .

