<https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/engagement_role_coding_v3> a nuproc:EngagementRoleCodingActivity ;
    rdfs:label "engagement role coding (protocol v3)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "In this demonstration graph no role claim or reference is linked to this activity: the role values and claims are synthetic and are generated by the synthetic activities."@en,
        "Multi-label coding of the engagement roles of the export-side actor in each of the 1,026 design events, whether or not the engagement took place, under a protocol and codebook frozen before coding (2026-10-14). All roles the evidence shows were recorded, with no priority rule; an event whose evidence showed no role was left without one. Each coded value is a role claim generated by this activity; outside the human-checked sample it is the final claim for that value. The same pass determined, for each event whose actor the dataset labels as a candidate set, which organization the article excerpts named; each determination is a resolution claim generated by this activity (ADR-0040, ADR-0043)."@en,
        "This coding stage does not reproduce: neither seed nor sampling temperature was exposed by the hosted model endpoint, and the harness version was not pinned (ADR-0003)."@en ;
    prov:qualifiedAssociation <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/engagement_role_coding_v3/association/codebook>,
        <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/engagement_role_coding_v3/association/prompt> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/agent/claude-opus-5-5> ;
    nuproc:usedCodebookVersion <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/codebook/v3.0> ;
    nuproc:usedPromptSpecification <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/prompt/engagement_role_coding-protocol-v3> .

