<https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/synthetic_clustering> a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "synthetic clustering"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Synthetic activity of the demonstration graph. The claims it generates are set by a fixed rule (scripts/build_public_demo.py): for the clusters of the synthetic sample, role values follow the event hash, every cluster is claimed to report an engagement that occurred, every reference to resolve to its synthetic organization and every identification to rest on the clustering key; eleven fixed branch examples show the other values. No model, coder or adjudicator took part, and the values model no real distribution."@en ;
    prov:qualifiedAssociation <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/synthetic_clustering/association/rule> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/agent/synthetic-demo-builder> .

<https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/synthetic_occurrence_coding> a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "synthetic occurrence coding"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Synthetic activity of the demonstration graph. The claims it generates are set by a fixed rule (scripts/build_public_demo.py): for the clusters of the synthetic sample, role values follow the event hash, every cluster is claimed to report an engagement that occurred, every reference to resolve to its synthetic organization and every identification to rest on the clustering key; eleven fixed branch examples show the other values. No model, coder or adjudicator took part, and the values model no real distribution."@en ;
    prov:qualifiedAssociation <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/synthetic_occurrence_coding/association/rule> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/agent/synthetic-demo-builder> .

<https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/synthetic_reference_resolution> a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "synthetic reference resolution"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Synthetic activity of the demonstration graph. The claims it generates are set by a fixed rule (scripts/build_public_demo.py): for the clusters of the synthetic sample, role values follow the event hash, every cluster is claimed to report an engagement that occurred, every reference to resolve to its synthetic organization and every identification to rest on the clustering key; eleven fixed branch examples show the other values. No model, coder or adjudicator took part, and the values model no real distribution."@en ;
    prov:qualifiedAssociation <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/activity/synthetic_reference_resolution/association/rule> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <https://w3id.org/nuproc/demo/agent/synthetic-demo-builder> .

<https://w3id.org/nuproc/rule/month-granularity> a nuproc:MonthGranularityRule ;
    rdfs:label "Month-granularity clustering rule"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Article-level engagements sharing the six-field key (case, channel, event subtype, leading actor, counterparty role, calendar month) are treated as one EngagementCluster. All event-level counts are conditional on this rule (ADR-0027)."@en .

